# Cursor MDC File Handling Standards

## Description

Establishes standards for safely creating and modifying MDC (Model-Driven Code) rule files while preserving metadata integrity and preventing corruption.

## Rule

1. File Creation Pattern:
   - MUST create new rules as .md first:

     ```shell
     # Create as .md initially
     touch .cursor/rules/my-rule.md
     ```

   - MUST include exact 5-line metadata header:

     ```markdown
     ---
     description: Brief description of the rule's purpose
     globs: ["pattern/to/match/*.ext"]
     alwaysApply: true
     ---
     ```

2. Metadata Handling:
   - MUST preserve metadata header format
   - MUST NOT add empty lines in metadata section
   - MUST NOT modify metadata structure
   - MUST include required fields:
     - description
     - globs
     - alwaysApply

3. File Conversion Process:
   - MUST verify metadata format before conversion
   - MUST use mv command for conversion:

     ```shell
     # Convert from .md to .mdc
     mv .cursor/rules/my-rule.md .cursor/rules/my-rule.mdc
     ```

4. Content Updates:
   - MUST create temporary .md for major changes
   - MUST preserve existing metadata when updating
   - MUST follow rename pattern for updates:

     ```shell
     # Update existing rule
     mv rule.mdc rule.md
     # Edit content
     mv rule.md rule.mdc
     ```

5. Metadata Validation:
   - MUST validate metadata before conversion:
     - Exact 5-line format
     - No empty lines
     - Required fields present
     - Valid YAML syntax

## Implementation

The Cursor IDE will:

- Enforce MDC file extension
- Validate metadata structure
- Prevent direct metadata modification
- Track file conversions
- Monitor content changes

## Benefits

- Prevents metadata corruption
- Maintains rule integrity
- Enables safe updates
- Preserves file structure
- Simplifies rule management
- Reduces editing errors
- Ensures format consistency

## Examples

✅ Correct:

```shell
# Creating new rule
echo "---
description: My new rule description
globs: [\"src/**/*.ts\"]
alwaysApply: true
---

# Rule Content" > .cursor/rules/new-rule.md

mv .cursor/rules/new-rule.md .cursor/rules/new-rule.mdc

# Updating existing rule
mv existing-rule.mdc existing-rule.md
# Edit content
mv existing-rule.md existing-rule.mdc
```

❌ Incorrect:

```shell
# Don't create .mdc directly
touch .cursor/rules/my-rule.mdc

# Don't modify metadata directly
sed -i '' 's/description:.*/description: new description/' rule.mdc

# Don't use wrong metadata format
echo "description: Invalid format
alwaysApply: true" > rule.mdc
```
